{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "There is no route deviation on this trip at all. Under POL-RD-01 the governing figure is the polyline length in the trace, not the rounded copy on the trip record: the trace measures 20.35 km against a booked optimal of 20.1 km, an excess of 0.25 km, or 1.24%. Both establishment gates must pass and neither does — 0.25 km is not greater than 20% of optimal (4.02 km), and it is not greater than 0.8 km. POL-RD-01 is explicit that if either test fails no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00535", "EV-TRIP-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The platform's own derived deviation block returns the status 'no deviation' for this trip, with excess_km 0.25 and excess_pct 1.2438%. The threshold and material-threshold fields it applies (0.8 km / 20% and 8.0 km / 50%) are never approached.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if any excess survived the gate, it is fully exonerated. The LTA DataMall advisory ADV-20261435-001 records a HIGH-severity multi-vehicle accident with two lanes closed on the SLE northbound near Lentor exit; that corridor intersects the route and the advisory window (06:36–07:56) overlaps the trip window (06:56–08:03). On POL-RD-03 the justified excess is min(measured 0.25 km, 1.30 x (22.8 - 20.1) + 1.0 = 4.51 km) = 0.25 km, so the entire measured excess is a justified closure avoidance and nothing is left to refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00535-01", "EV-GPS-00535", "EV-TRIP-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.justified_excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the excess is fully exonerated as an external event under POL-RD-03, the distance and time charges stand — the driver is not at fault for the accident. POL-RD-09(2) confirms that on a POL-RD-03 exoneration the distance and time charges are kept and only off-route ERP is corrected as a pass-through; here the fare breakdown carries 0.00 of ERP and 0.00 of tolls, so there is nothing to correct in any event.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00535", "EV-ADVIS-00535-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 67-minute duration against a 44-minute optimal is a traffic-delay effect, not a longer route. The driver's trace, 403 fixes at a 10-second cadence with 100% coverage and no gaps, never leaves the optimal corridor by more than 0.25 km, and the delay window coincides exactly with the accident advisory. Time lost in queued or slow traffic is not excess distance under POL-RD-01, and the rider's claim is built on elapsed time, not on the distance the policy measures.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00535", "EV-TRIP-00535", "EV-ADVIS-00535-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The closure-adjusted recomputation shown in the fare breakdown's derived block does not generate a refund. POL-RD-02 runs only 'where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01 and no exculpatory clause fully excuses it'; no deviation is established on this trace, and POL-RD-03 fully excuses the only 0.25 km that exists, so the POL-RD-02 arithmetic is not triggered and the metered charge on the ledger stands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00535", "EV-GPS-00535", "EV-ADVIS-00535-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation pattern exists to uplift anything. On POL-RD-06 the relevant counters are driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d, which is 0, against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d, which is 250; that is below both the 3-flag test and the 0.05-ratio test, so neither the FULL_REFUND uplift of POL-RD-06(b) nor the conduct referral of POL-RD-06(c) is licensed. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is not the trailing-90-day field this test names and cannot be substituted.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The loss the rider presses — a missed train and roughly $200 of consequential change costs — is not a route-deviation remedy. POL-RD-02 makes any refund arithmetic against the fare breakdown rather than discretionary damages, and the ledger records a metered total charged of SGD 38.66 with no refund issued. A small or large consequential loss outside the fare cannot be recovered through this policy.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.charged_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This dispute was filed by the rider and the present state is a live charge (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). Under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION is party-relative: it leaves that state exactly as it stands, which on a rider-filed claim that the evidence does not support is the driver-favourable outcome and keeps the fare the driver earned.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00535"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
